  "lineage": "Traditional music of the Basque Country on both sides of the Pyrenees, catalogued by Resurrección María de Azkue and Aita Donostia in the 1910s-20s and revived from the 1970s by Oskorri and Kepa Junkera — narrow-range modal melodies sung in Euskara, txistu-and-tamboril one-man pipe-and-drum for processional dances, double-reed alboka with circular breathing, txalaparta plank duo in interlocking irregular strokes, and dance repertoire (aurresku, fandango, arin-arin) alternating 6/8 and 2/4 with strong stepped accents.",
